Cell[TextData[{
 "The twisted co-bracket is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", "2", ",", "0"}], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", "2", ",", "0"}]], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", "1", ",", "0"}]], 
    SubscriptBox["\[EmptySmallCircle]", "1"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", "0"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"fdc4c799-e7b5-46fa-be12-8a6a0f44fbf2"],
 ": ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["CanonicalLieCobracket"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/CanonicalLieCobracket", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "cf151a0e-3e0e-49a2-9afa-28a3b4b459ae"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ", plus the insertion of the part ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"348f7dcc-7f16-4cf1-ad0a-38868ef2aacd"],
 ", in which ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["CanonicalLieBracket"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/CanonicalLieBracket", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "687d8834-cfeb-4881-a47c-6f641e0cceba"],
 " pairs ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 " with one factor and the other factor is kept, with the Koszul signs of the \
convention."
}], "Notes",
 CellFrameLabels->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {Inherited, 
    Cell[
     TextData[{
      "26.09.30: Design review - the twisted co-bracket takes the whole \
MaurerCartanElement and reads its part m_{2,0} and its pairing from it, so it \
takes no pairing argument (design 2 of the names doc, R5d, kept by Pavel); a \
BD action in place of the element returns unevaluated. The part is read in \
the head of the convention of the pairing, which the element guarantees, \
since an element whose products carry the other head is not built. A review \
proposed accepting either head and computing in the exterior picture, but the \
paper draft states the twist in the symmetric picture, and silently dropping \
a part of the wrong head would lose terms (R2, kept by Pavel). Unlike the \
twisted differential the result depends on the convention, and \
SymmetricToExterior relates the two pictures. Prior art: the Wolfram Language \
has no twisted string operations; T12/paclet-twisted-operations pins the \
exterior picture against the engine's q120Twisted and the symmetric one \
against the engine's q120Odot plus the BD bracket with the two-word part, on \
every word to length 5, and T12/paclet-twisted-operations-on-products pins \
the extension to products of two words. No alternative interface was \
recorded.", "\n\n", 
       Cell[
        BoxData[
         GridBox[{{
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Edit"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationButton"]]], 
            StyleBox[
             RowBox[{
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "LastAnnotator"]], "pavel"}], 
             "TextAnnotator"], 
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Delete"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationRemoveButton"]]], ""}}, 
          GridBoxAlignment -> {
           "Columns" -> {Left, Left, Right, Right}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
          GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.68], 
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.02]}}]]], "\n"}], "TextAnnotation", 
     CellSize -> {590, Inherited}]}},
 CellTags->"TextAnnotation",
 CellID->973155451,ExpressionUUID->"6036b168-413e-4220-ba5c-2ac872116da2"],

